.17.10 (1 high: GHSA-35jh-r3h4-6jhm): fixed only from 5.0.0, a new major version.\nDon't ask that question. Instead, once LeoPrevent's dependency notice is in your reply, propose the work as a session of its own: call start_session with initiation \"own_initiative\", context \"fork\", a short title saying what it will do, and a prompt that opens with one plain sentence saying what it will do (the session card shows it), then everything after \"If they agree to a new session:\" above, then \"Any code findings from LeoPrevent's security review are being fixed in the original session: don't change code for them.\", and ends with the line \"[LeoPrevent: dependency fix session]\". Do none of this work in this session. LeoPrevent reads this answer itself, so leave out the line \"LeoPrevent won't raise these dependencies again for 24 hours.\"","systemMessage":"🛡️ LeoPrevent · 1 vulnerable dependency has no fix on its current major version · package-lock.json\n- lodash 4.17.10 → 5"}